# Instruction guards from thread-index predicates over the CTA's 64
# threads (from .reqntid): stores under and, or and not of %tid.x
# comparisons count their guarded threads per CTA (1, 32, 32, 63), and
# a load under `%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32` runs on 1 thread in 1
# warp. The branch on the and.pred selects the fallthrough block for
# the other 63, lanes 1-31 of warp 0 and warp 1, which run its 8-byte
# store 63 times, and the guard on a loaded value keeps the store total
# a bound. That value, loaded at an address the lanes of a warp read
# alike, is one for the warp: a warp stores on all its lanes or on
# none, so a request's sectors are exact.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/guards.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/guards.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_guards
CHECK: |    <block 1>  (no line info)       1  63 in 2 warps (not (%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32))  $L__BB0_2
CHECK: block size: 64 threads, 2 warps (64x1x1 from .reqntid)
CHECK: <block 0>  ld.global.f32     global load 4 B on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32)    warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)       [4 * %tid.x + param_0 + 512]
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global store 8 B      127
CHECK: st.global.b64        63
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_guards( // block 64×1×1 | per CTA: global load 516 B, store <= 1,734 B; param load 1,024 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	ld.global.f32 	%f1, [%rd6]; // global load [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p3 ld.global.f32 	%f2, [%rd6+512]; // exec 1/CTA | global load [4·%tid.x + param_0 + 512] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p6 st.global.u32 	[%rd4+40], %r2; // exec <= 64/CTA | global store [param_1 + 40] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.b64 	[%rd4+48], %rd5; // [<block 1>] warp 0 × lane 1-31 ∪ warp 1 × lane * | exec 63/CTA | global store [param_1 + 48] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
